1 | web-frontend | Branch feat/w2-risk-tiers from origin/main after PR 94 has merged (rebase if it merged while you work). Read docs/proposals/fleet-optimization.md section 5 W2. ONE, docs/risk-tiers.md: the tier table. Tier A: money, identity, security, data retention. Tier B: traveller-facing product. Tier C: internal tooling and docs. For each tier: the critic set (Tier A: domain critic plus security-reviewer plus api-critic when a contract changes; Tier B: domain critic plus frontend-critic when a page changes; Tier C: one critic), the round cap before a recorded merge-or-stop decision (Tier A: 4, Tier B: 3, Tier C: 2, the Tier C cap is the owner decision of 2026-09-14 10:25; the A and B caps are proposals marked for owner confirmation), what counts as a blocking finding (Tier A: any correctness, security or contract finding; Tier B: any user-visible defect or contract drift; Tier C: only a finding that makes the tool wrong or misleading, everything else is filed as an issue), and the critic model tier (unchanged routing for all tiers in this PR). TWO, the plan format: a TIER: A, B or C header line, documented in README next to the other headers. THREE, scripts/dispatch.sh stops before starting a plan with no TIER header, naming the rule, and prints the tier in the dispatch banner; an ALLOW-NO-TIER header lets the owner override. FOUR, the ledger (if PR 96 has merged) reads the TIER header; if PR 96 has not merged, leave a note in the PR body. Tests in tests/run-plan-check-tests.sh: a plan without TIER is refused; with TIER C it passes; ALLOW-NO-TIER passes; the banner names the tier. VERIFY: tests/run-plan-check-tests.sh only, real exit code in the PR body; no full suite. HOUSE STYLE: no long dash anywhere, no AI tool or vendor name, no Co-Authored-By trailer. Open a draft PR titled Fleet optimization W2: risk tiers. | feat/w2-risk-tiers

2 | plan-critic | READ-ONLY REVIEW of the PR on branch feat/w2-risk-tiers. Tier C, round 1 of at most 2. No commits, no push, no review, no labels; tmp writes only. Record head SHA at start and at report. Check the tier table is unambiguous for real plans (classify the last ten plans under wave-plans by the table and report any that fit two tiers), the check refuses a plan without TIER and cannot be bypassed by a lower-case or indented header, and the A and B caps are marked for owner confirmation. Report only findings that make the tiers ambiguous or the check bypassable. Post ONE comment on the PR whose first line reads CRITIC W2 RISK TIERS with SAFE-TO-MERGE, BLOCK-FIX or BLOCK-ESCALATE and citations. HOUSE STYLE: no long dash, no AI tool or vendor name. | feat/w2-risk-tiers
